# The line `int: x 5` writes what stands in its slot when it runs (the author 2026-11-11, R12; plan M11 5a, B5): the
# first launch of Self finds 5 there and adds 1, publishing 6; the second finds the published 6 and gives 7.
Self:
    int: x 5
    x := x + 1
end: Self
call: Self
int: first Self\x
call: Self
int: second Self\x
